 community</article-title><source>Soc Psychiatry Psychiatr Epidemiol</source><year>2004</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>259</fpage><lpage>264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15085326</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00127-004-0736-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bebbington</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Meltzer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Brugha</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Farrell</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jenkins</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ceresa</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Unequal access and unmet need: neurotic disorders and the use of primary care services (Reprinted from Psychological Medicine, vol 30, pgs 1359&#x02013;1367, 2000)</article-title><source>International Review of Psychiatry</source><year>2003</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>122</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12745318</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/0954026021000046029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oliver</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Coe</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunnell</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Help-seeking behaviour in men and women with common mental health problems: cross-sectional study</article-title><source>British Journal of Psychiatry</source><year>2005</year><volume>186</volume><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15802685</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1192/bjp.186.4.297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paykel</surname><given-names>ES</given-names></name><name><surname>Hart</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Priest</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changes in public attitudes to depression during the Defeat Depression Campaign</article-title><source>British Journal of Psychiatry</source><year>1998</year><volume>173</volume><fpage>519</fpage><lpage>522</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9926082</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Commander</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cochrane</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sashidharan</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Akilu</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Wildsmith</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mental health care for Asian, black and white patients with non-affective psychoses: pathways to the psychiatric hospital, in-patient and after-care</article-title><source>Social Psychiatry and Psychiatric Epidemiology</source><year>1999</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>484</fpage><lpage>491</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10541669</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s001270050224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>Snowden</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name><name><surname>Sue</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><source>Differences between Asian and White Americans' help seeking and utilization patterns in the Los Angeles area</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>US: Lawrence Erlbaum Assoc.</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abe-Kim</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictors of help seeking for emotional distress among Chinese Americans: family matters</article-title><source>J Consult Clin Psychol</source><year>2002</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>1186</fpage><lpage>1190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12362969</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-006X.70.5.1186</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kleinman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Patients and Healers in the Context of Culture</source><year>1980</year><publisher-name>Berkeley and Los Angeles: University of California Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jorm</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Population promotion of informal self-help strategies for early intervention against depression and anxiety</article-title><source>Psychol Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16356291</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0033291705005659</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cauce</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Domenech-Rodriguez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Paradise</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cochran</surname><given-names>BN</given-names></name><name><surname>Shea</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><sur